Login prompt bottom-left, frameless; clock bottom-right.

Applied to qylock's pixel-hollowknight Main.qml by sddm/customise-theme.sh
--layout bottom-left. A patch rather than a copy of the file: qylock is GPL-3
and this repo is MIT, and a diff of only these edits keeps the two apart.

  - login block  ->  anchors.left + anchors.bottom, no panel, no hanging line
  - password     ->  one underline instead of a full border, left-aligned
  - clock        ->  bottom right; its Row is anchored rather than centred,
                     because the Item it lives in has no width and centring it
                     against the right edge pushed the time off screen
  - a bottom gradient, so frameless text stays readable over the video

If a qylock update changes Main.qml this will refuse to apply; redo it from
the new file rather than forcing it.

--- a/Main.qml
+++ b/Main.qml
@@ -38,6 +38,19 @@
 
     Loader { anchors.fill: parent; source: "BackgroundVideo.qml" }
 
+    // Readability wash. The prompt is frameless and sits straight on the
+    // video, which has a lightning strike in it. Delete this one Rectangle to
+    // remove the effect; nothing else depends on it.
+    Rectangle {
+        anchors.left: parent.left; anchors.right: parent.right; anchors.bottom: parent.bottom
+        height: parent.height * 0.45
+        gradient: Gradient {
+            GradientStop { position: 0.0; color: "#00000000" }
+            GradientStop { position: 0.55; color: "#77000000" }
+            GradientStop { position: 1.0; color: "#dd000000" }
+        }
+    }
